# The README demo, as a script rather than a recording.
#
#   vhs docs/demo.tape        →  docs/demo.gif
#
# A hand-recorded GIF is stale the first time the CLI output changes and nobody
# notices until a reader points at a column that no longer exists. This is
# regenerated by one command, so keeping it honest costs nothing.
#
# vhs: https://github.com/charmbracelet/vhs  (go install github.com/charmbracelet/vhs@latest)
#
# Every Sleep carries an explicit unit. A bare number is read as seconds, so
# `Sleep 1200` written meaning "1.2 seconds" is twenty minutes of vhs sitting
# at a blank prompt with no indication anything is wrong.
#
# The sequence is chosen to make one point in under fifteen seconds: WebFetch
# gets nothing from this page, and sieve gets the site. Everything else is cut.

Output docs/demo.gif

Set Shell bash
Set FontSize 17
Set Width 1180
Set Height 620
Set Padding 22
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set PlaybackSpeed 1.0

# --- What a plain fetch sees -------------------------------------------------
Type "# igloo.inc serves an empty <body>. Everything is drawn in WebGL."
Enter
Sleep 1200ms

Type "curl -s https://igloo.inc | tr -d '[:space:]' | wc -c"
Enter
Sleep 2500ms

Type "# Fourteen characters. No words at all. This is what WebFetch gets."
Enter
Sleep 1800ms

Ctrl+L

# --- What sieve sees ---------------------------------------------------------
Type "sieve distill https://igloo.inc"
Enter

# Wait for the run to finish rather than guessing at it. A fixed sleep is
# wrong in both directions here: igloo.inc takes anywhere from fifteen to
# thirty-five seconds depending on how long its scene takes to build and how
# patiently the sweep waits for text that is never coming, so a short sleep
# clips the output and a long one records dead air. The regexp matches the
# last line the command prints.
Wait+Screen@60s /total/

Type "# 29 blocks, read out of the 3D scene. 40 of 40 ground-truth facts."
Enter
Sleep 2000ms

Ctrl+L

Type "head -24 artifacts/igloo.inc/index.md"
Enter
Sleep 5000ms

Sleep 2500ms
